{"availability":"available","full":"linlin1451/backward-harmony","name":"backward-harmony","description":"Write chord progressions backward from the final chord. Weighted common-practice rules plus authentic, plagal, deceptive, half and tritone-substitute cadences into any chord; borrowed and secondary chords, inversions, split bars, playback and MIDI export. Plain JavaScript, runs on GitHub Pages.","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-06T04:21:46Z","updated":"2026-10-06T20:52:45Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://linlin1451.github.io/backward-harmony/","topics":["algorithmic-composition","chord-progression","generative-music","github-pages","harmony","javascript","midi","music-theory","web-audio"],"demo":"https://linlin1451.github.io/backward-harmony/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:03:55.085Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T07:03:55.085Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T07:03:55.085Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:03:55.085Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A browser app that writes chord progressions backward. It fixes the last chord first, then chooses every earlier chord from weighted rules and from the cadences that can lead into the chord after it. You can play the result, edit any chord, and download it as MIDI.","It's plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript modules, with no build step and no dependencies. Push it to GitHub and it deploys itself to GitHub Pages."],"features":["Backward derivation, one chord per bar. The generator writes only the first chord of each bar, choosing it from the weighted options that can come before what follows. Your own choices stay fixed when you generate again.","Bars and parts. The bars are shown four to a row. Any bar can be divided into two to four equal parts. New parts hold the bar's chord until you pick a different chord for them. If you pick one, the bar's first chord is…","One tile per distinct chord. When parts of a bar repeat the same chord, the chord is shown once, stretched across those parts. The small numbered strip under it marks each part; click a number to change that part.","Undo and redo. Every change can be undone (Undo button, Ctrl+Z or ⌘Z) to bring back the previous progression, and redone (Redo, Ctrl+Shift+Z or ⌘⇧Z).","Held repeats. When a part repeats the chord before it in the same bar (same chord, same inversion), playback and MIDI hold the chord instead of striking it again. Mark a part \"Play it again here\" in the editor to…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/linlin1451/backward-harmony/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"e06d440c80b769743386c143e3b6f49857d74081a44233bf0fb2133723c4a9c8","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T07:03:55.175Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:03:55.175Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A browser app that writes chord progressions backward. It fixes the last chord first, then chooses every earlier chord from weighted rules and from the cadences that can lead into the chord after it. You can play the result, edit any chord, and download it as MIDI.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/linlin1451/backward-harmony/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"e06d440c80b769743386c143e3b6f49857d74081a44233bf0fb2133723c4a9c8","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/linlin1451/backward-harmony/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T07:03:55.175Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-06T20:52:45Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/linlin1451/backward-harmony/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T07:03:55.176Z","hash":"e06d440c80b769743386c143e3b6f49857d74081a44233bf0fb2133723c4a9c8","originalBytes":6770,"storedBytes":6770,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["chord","chords","any","bar","github","software","src","git","one","key","open","pages","run","same","backward","bash","before","copyright","every","first","inversion","it.